            <ArticleTitle>A new technique to anchor stents for exact placement in ostial stenoses: the stent tail wire or Szabo technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>901-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a technique for correct positioning of a stent in an ostial stenosis by using a second wire passed through the last cell of a stent. The anchor wire technique, first described by Szabo et al. [Szabo S, Abramowitz B, Vaitkus PT. Am J Cardiol 2005;96:212H], will facilitate precise ostial stent placement and eliminate errors of positioning inside or outside the ostial narrowing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
